# Git start — no Linear

Do not wait for Linear, a Linear issue ID, or a paste from Linear. That workflow is retired.

When the user asks to implement, fix, or ship code:

1. If not already on a matching feature branch, create one from up-to-date `main`:
   `git checkout main && git pull && git checkout -b ej/<short-kebab-slug>`
2. Slug = the work in a few words. No ticket number required.
   - Good: `ej/tenancy-lilac-backfill`, `ej/elilai-product-waitlist`
   - Bad: `ej/esp-201-...` only because Linear used that — do not invent Linear IDs
3. Then make the changes on that branch. Commit / PR / merge only when the user asks.

Do not create GitHub Issues unless the user asks. A branch name is enough to start.
